// Silent sound carrier — the reload chime, and the canonical example of the
// shape every other snd_*.json5 in here copies.
//
// WHY A PARTICLE AT ALL. The §11 weapon trigger lists (`on.dryfire`,
// `on.reload`, `on.reloading`, `on.selected`, …) execute `emit` and nothing
// else, exactly like `on.fire` — a weapon cannot call the `sound` verb
// itself. So the shortest legal handoff from a trigger to a sound is an
// invisible particle that fuses immediately and plays the sound on its way
// out. Same trick as particles/gadget.json5 uses to reach `spawn_body`.
//
// INVISIBLE BY CONSTRUCTION, two independent ways, because one of them
// silently stops being true if someone adds art here later:
//   - no `presentation.sprite`, so the render sprite-start resolves to the
//     -1 sentinel and this def gets no sprite set at all;
//   - no `presentation.color_index`, which means 0, and the point-render
//     pass skips colour 0 as "no palette entry".
//
// INERT BY CONSTRUCTION. radius 0, speed 0, gravity 0, no `collide_worm` and
// no `collide_terrain` list, and the wallhack bounce so terrain can never
// park or detonate it. It spawns ~5px off the muzzle, sits there for its two
// ticks, and expires. `fuse.ticks: 1` is the shortest expressible fuse (a
// wObject-class def expires on `time_alive > timeout`).
//
// AND YET IT MUST STAY IN THE SIM — that is the whole point, and it is not an
// accident. The engine's R11 fast path demotes consequence-free particles to
// the render-side fx pool, skipping the world spawn entirely; a particle that
// got demoted would never play anything. `is_fx_only` reads a `sound` verb as
// a consequence, so this def is never demoted, the spawn is real, and the
// SoundEvent goes out at the muzzle **on every peer**. That is why the reload
// hook lives here rather than in a client-side reaction to a weapon's
// `presentation.sounds.reload`: you hear the enemy's magazine, not just your
// own.
{
  "legacy": {
    "wallhack_bounce": -1
  },
  "physics": {
    "gravity": 0,
    "damping": 1,
    "wobble": 0,
    "pushed_by_blasts": false,
    "ccd": false,
    "substeps": 1
  },
  "radius": 0,
  "collide": {
    "terrain": false,
    "worms": false,
    "projectiles": false
  },
  "fuse": {
    "ticks": 1,
    "variance": 0
  },
  "on": {
    "fuse": [
      {
        "sound": {
          "file": "reloaded.wav"
        }
      },
      {
        "remove": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "speed": 0
}
